{"path":"std/sync/mpsc/index.html","title":"Module mpsc","description":"Multi-producer, single-consumer FIFO queue communication primitives.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module mpsc"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/sync/mpsc.rs.html#1-1261","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-producer, single-consumer FIFO queue communication primitives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module provides message-based communication over channels, concretely defined among three types:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Sender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Sender"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.SyncSender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::SyncSender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyncSender"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Sender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Sender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Sender"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.SyncSender.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::SyncSender","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"SyncSender"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is used to send data to a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Both senders are clone-able (multi-producer) such that many threads can send simultaneously to one receiver (single-consumer)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These channels come in two flavors:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An asynchronous, infinitely buffered channel. The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpsc::channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function will return a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(Sender, Receiver)"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple where all sends will be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"asynchronous"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (they never block). The channel conceptually has an infinite buffer."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A synchronous, bounded channel. The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.sync_channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sync_channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function will return a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(SyncSender, Receiver)"},{"type":"text","value":" tuple where the storage for pending messages is a pre-allocated buffer of a fixed size. All sends will be "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"synchronous"}]},{"type":"text","value":" by blocking until there is buffer space available. Note that a bound of 0 is allowed, causing the channel to become a “rendezvous” channel where each sender atomically hands off a message to a receiver."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"disconnection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disconnection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The send and receive operations on channels will all return a "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html","title":"enum std::result::Result","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" indicating whether the operation succeeded or not. An unsuccessful operation is normally indicative of the other half of a channel having “hung up” by being dropped in its corresponding thread."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once half of a channel has been deallocated, most operations can no longer continue to make progress, so "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#variant.Err","title":"variant std::result::Result::Err","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Err"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will be returned. Many applications will continue to "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#method.unwrap","title":"method std::result::Result::unwrap","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"unwrap"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the results returned from this module, instigating a propagation of failure among threads if one unexpectedly dies."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Simple usage:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpsc::channel;\n\n// Create a simple streaming channel\nlet (tx, rx) = channel();\nthread::spawn(move || {\n    tx.send(10).unwrap();\n});\nassert_eq!(rx.recv().unwrap(), 10);"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++use+std::sync::mpsc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++//+Create+a+simple+streaming+channel%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel();%0A++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++tx.send(10).unwrap();%0A++++%7D);%0A++++assert_eq!(rx.recv().unwrap(),+10);%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared usage:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpsc::channel;\n\n// Create a shared channel that can be sent along from many threads\n// where tx is the sending half (tx for transmission), and rx is the receiving\n// half (rx for receiving).\nlet (tx, rx) = channel();\nfor i in 0..10 {\n    let tx = tx.clone();\n    thread::spawn(move || {\n        tx.send(i).unwrap();\n    });\n}\n\nfor _ in 0..10 {\n    let j = rx.recv().unwrap();\n    assert!(0 <= j && j < 10);\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++use+std::sync::mpsc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++//+Create+a+shared+channel+that+can+be+sent+along+from+many+threads%0A++++//+where+tx+is+the+sending+half+(tx+for+transmission),+and+rx+is+the+receiving%0A++++//+half+(rx+for+receiving).%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel();%0A++++for+i+in+0..10+%7B%0A++++++++let+tx+=+tx.clone();%0A++++++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++++++tx.send(i).unwrap();%0A++++++++%7D);%0A++++%7D%0A++++%0A++++for+_+in+0..10+%7B%0A++++++++let+j+=+rx.recv().unwrap();%0A++++++++assert!(0+%3C=+j+%26%26+j+%3C+10);%0A++++%7D%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Propagating panics:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::sync::mpsc::channel;\n\n// The call to recv() will return an error because the channel has already\n// hung up (or been deallocated)\nlet (tx, rx) = channel::<i32>();\ndrop(tx);\nassert!(rx.recv().is_err());"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::sync::mpsc::channel;%0A++++%0A++++//+The+call+to+recv()+will+return+an+error+because+the+channel+has+already%0A++++//+hung+up+(or+been+deallocated)%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+channel::%3Ci32%3E();%0A++++drop(tx);%0A++++assert!(rx.recv().is_err());%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synchronous channels:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\nuse std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel;\n\nlet (tx, rx) = sync_channel::<i32>(0);\nthread::spawn(move || {\n    // This will wait for the parent thread to start receiving\n    tx.send(53).unwrap();\n});\nrx.recv().unwrap();"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++use+std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel;%0A++++%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+sync_channel::%3Ci32%3E(0);%0A++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++//+This+will+wait+for+the+parent+thread+to+start+receiving%0A++++++++tx.send(53).unwrap();%0A++++%7D);%0A++++rx.recv().unwrap();%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unbounded receive loop:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel;\nuse std::thread;\n\nlet (tx, rx) = sync_channel(3);\n\nfor _ in 0..3 {\n    // It would be the same without thread and clone here\n    // since there will still be one `tx` left.\n    let tx = tx.clone();\n    // cloned tx dropped within thread\n    thread::spawn(move || tx.send(\"ok\").unwrap());\n}\n\n// Drop the last sender to stop `rx` waiting for message.\n// The program will not complete if we comment this out.\n// **All** `tx` needs to be dropped for `rx` to have `Err`.\ndrop(tx);\n\n// Unbounded receiver waiting for all senders to complete.\nwhile let Ok(msg) = rx.recv() {\n    println!(\"{msg}\");\n}\n\nprintln!(\"completed\");"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel;%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++%0A++++let+(tx,+rx)+=+sync_channel(3);%0A++++%0A++++for+_+in+0..3+%7B%0A++++++++//+It+would+be+the+same+without+thread+and+clone+here%0A++++++++//+since+there+will+still+be+one+%60tx%60+left.%0A++++++++let+tx+=+tx.clone();%0A++++++++//+cloned+tx+dropped+within+thread%0A++++++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+tx.send(%22ok%22).unwrap());%0A++++%7D%0A++++%0A++++//+Drop+the+last+sender+to+stop+%60rx%60+waiting+for+message.%0A++++//+The+program+will+not+complete+if+we+comment+this+out.%0A++++//+**All**+%60tx%60+needs+to+be+dropped+for+%60rx%60+to+have+%60Err%60.%0A++++drop(tx);%0A++++%0A++++//+Unbounded+receiver+waiting+for+all+senders+to+complete.%0A++++while+let+Ok(msg)+=+rx.recv()+%7B%0A++++++++println!(%22%7Bmsg%7D%22);%0A++++%7D%0A++++%0A++++println!(%22completed%22);%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"structs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structs"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.IntoIter.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::IntoIter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"IntoIter"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An owning iterator over messages on a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":", created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.into_iter","title":"method std::sync::mpsc::Receiver::into_iter","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"into_iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Iter.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Iter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Iter"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An iterator over messages on a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":", created by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.iter","title":"method std::sync::mpsc::Receiver::iter","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"iter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Receiver"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"The receiving half of Rust’s "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpsc::channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/fn.sync_channel.html","title":"fn std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sync_channel"}]},{"type":"text","value":") type. This half can only be owned by one thread."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.RecvError.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::RecvError","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RecvError"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An error returned from the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html#method.recv","title":"method std::sync::mpsc::Receiver::recv","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"recv"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function on a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.Receiver.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::Receiver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Receiver"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/mpsc/struct.SendError.html","title":"struct std::sync::mpsc::SendError","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SendError"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An error returned from the "},{"type"